---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'About Which Deadly Sin: Method, Author & Editorial Stance';
const description =
  'Meet the author and method behind the Which Deadly Sin quiz: how the 15-question seven deadly sins test is built, scored, and kept independent.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/about/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-11-19"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
    ]}
  />

  <article class="prose-article mt-4">
    <h1>About Which Deadly Sin</h1>

    <h2>Who writes this site</h2>
    <p>
      This site is written and maintained by <strong>{SITE.author.name}</strong>,{' '}
      {SITE.author.bio} The seven deadly sins framework has been used for more than fifteen
      hundred years as a tool for examining character, and this project exists to make that tool
      usable in a five-minute browser session.
    </p>

    <h2>How the quiz is built</h2>
    <p>
      The quiz contains <strong>15 statements</strong>. Pride is covered by three statements and
      the other six dimensions &mdash; envy, wrath, sloth, greed, gluttony, and lust &mdash; by
      two each. Every statement is answered on a four-point scale from <em>strongly disagree</em>
      (0 points) to <em>strongly agree</em> (3 points).
    </p>
    <p>
      Scores are normalized per dimension: your points are divided by the maximum points available
      for that dimension and expressed as a percentage. This means the dimension with three
      questions is not advantaged over the dimensions with two. Your dominant sin is the dimension
      with the highest percentage; ties follow the traditional ordering that begins with pride.
    </p>
    <p>
      All scoring runs <strong>locally in your browser</strong>. The site has no server-side
      application, no database, and no user accounts. Your answers are never transmitted or stored,
      which is also why the quiz needs no login and no email address.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial stance and limitations</h2>
    <p>
      This is an editorial and educational project, not a clinical instrument. The seven deadly
      sins are a historical and ethical framework; the quiz is not based on a validated
      psychological assessment such as the Big Five inventory and{' '}
      <strong>
        does not constitute psychological, psychiatric, or medical diagnosis or treatment
      </strong>
      . If you are dealing with distress, compulsive behavior, or relationship harm, please consult
      a licensed professional.
    </p>
    <p>
      Content is reviewed against established historical sources &mdash; primarily the writings of
      Evagrius Ponticus, John Cassian, Gregory I, Thomas Aquinas, and Dante Alighieri &mdash; and
      updated when errors are found. Corrections can be sent to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
    <p>
      The site is free to use and currently carries no advertising and no paid placements. If
      affiliate or sponsored links are ever introduced, they will be disclosed on the page where
      they appear and will never influence the quiz or its scoring.
    </p>

    <p>
      Start with the <a href="/">seven deadly sins test on the homepage</a> or read the full{' '}
      <a href="/seven-deadly-sins/">seven deadly sins guide</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
